This identifies the root cause.

You have two independent conditions that together are blocking SR-IOV configuration.

1. Master MCP is paused

You confirmed:

oc get machineconfigpool master -o jsonpath='{.spec.paused}'
true

This is the first problem.

When the SR-IOV operator adds kernel arguments:

intel_iommu=on

iommu=pt


it creates a MachineConfig and expects the Machine Config Operator (MCO) to apply it.

Because the master MCP is paused, the MachineConfig cannot be applied.


---

2. Node is permanently cordoned

Your node is:

Ready,SchedulingDisabled
Unschedulable: true

Since this is an SNO cluster, there is only one node. The SR-IOV operator has drained and cordoned the node and is waiting for the reboot/update to finish.

That's why you see:

SriovNetworkNodeState

Desired Sync State : Reboot_Required
Current Sync State : Draining

and

CSV: Installing

The new operator pod stays Pending because the only node is unschedulable.


---

Fix

Step 1: Unpause the master MCP

oc patch mcp master --type=merge -p '{"spec":{"paused":false}}'

Verify:

oc get mcp master

Paused should become false.


---

Step 2: Wait a few minutes

Watch:

oc get mcp -w

and

oc get co machine-config

The MachineConfig Operator should begin reconciling.


---

Step 3: If the node is still cordoned after MCO finishes

Uncordon it:

oc adm uncordon sno1.lab1.ocp.lan


---

Step 4: Watch SR-IOV recover

oc get sriovnetworknodestate -w

You should eventually see:

SYNC STATUS            Succeeded
CURRENT SYNC STATE     Succeeded

Then check:

oc get csv -n openshift-sriov-network-operator

The phase should change from:

Installing

to

Succeeded


---

One thing I want to verify

Before you unpause the MCP, please run these two commands:

oc get machineconfig | grep -i sriov

and

oc get machineconfigpool master

If there is a pending SR-IOV MachineConfig waiting to be applied, unpausing the MCP should allow the update to complete and resolve the SR-IOV operator installation.
